y><entry><title>China: English to be removed as a graded core subject?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:17723f0e4d5d9acb58bf2b7cb5cd76525edef839001b72a779f58226a392d973</id><updated>2026-09-10T12:59:09Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T19:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/china-english-to-be-removed-as-a-graded-core-subject/a-79199629--52f7a1cb9d3e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/china-english-to-be-removed-as-a-graded-core-subject/a-79199629?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A university professor is calling for English to no longer be taught as a graded core subject in Chinese schools. Opponents argue that, in a globalized world, knowing English benefits the country and one's career.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Cambodia's floating schools hit by rising fuel costs</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:938a89829530923526f6ff9795616aaaf1bc50e341606b047fc46ff7d0e73f9e</id><updated>2026-09-10T12:59:09Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T12:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/cambodia-s-floating-schools-hit-by-rising-fuel-costs/a-79202008--dc2e9aeeea22.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/cambodia-s-floating-schools-hit-by-rising-fuel-costs/a-79202008?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Iran war has sent fuel prices higher in Cambodia, squeezing families who rely on fishing and boats for their livelihoods. For children living on Tonle Sap, rising fuel costs pose yet another barrier to education.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>The billion-euro trade driving Europe's eels to extinction</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:63a01d78ddaa24d4f4d80db4d3fd33ad06cf9f4f95cdef512784b2e3c1b1fc65</id><updated>2026-09-10T12:59:09Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T08:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-billion-euro-trade-drivi