frican trafficking victims in the Asian country with no money, no passport and no prospects.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>How Mao Zedong's legacy still shapes China 50 years on</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:73bcb6e9545d5167a6a45c347fb0556726ed33c3ed08ec1802437087429c6b38</id><updated>2026-09-10T12:59:09Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T14:44:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-mao-zedong-s-legacy-still-shapes-china-50-years-on/a-79189751--83b4fb70b8d5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-mao-zedong-s-legacy-still-shapes-china-50-years-on/a-79189751?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">China has transformed since Mao Zedong's death 50 years ago. But his legacy endures — from Xi Jinping's rule to a new wave of Mao nostalgia among young Chinese.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Japan's empty temples seek new ways to survive</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9a3d078390c946e32e8bb972111540b88f1f3bd46e322a9be0a7ec2e71ee751e</id><updated>2026-09-10T12:59:09Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T12:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/japan-s-empty-temples-seek-new-ways-to-survive/a-79157964--7eea677a26bf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/japan-s-empty-temples-seek-new-ways-to-survive/a-79157964?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">With a declining population, shrinking congregations and growing economic pressures, temples are struggling to stay relevant. As more temples are sold or closed, is religion in decline in modern Japan?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Afghanistan's women: A national soccer team without a home</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f719fc0e9b0b3d9ebe18e91a023f58564bc7940c6038ae1d64c8cc4316ce9561</id><updated>2026-09-10T12:59:09Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T11:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../